<title>JAPAN: Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo oil products market is closed for a national holiday on Monday.</p>
<p>Trade will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, naphtha prices climbed for the third day running, gaining support from firmer European markets.</p>
<p>Open-spec naphtha for second-half September was assessed at about $213.00 per tonne, up from Thursday's $210.50.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-3432-8837</p>
</text>
